{
  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.512 acc outperforms config_001 (same but transformer aggregation) at 0.471 acc, establishing avgpool as the preferred aggregation for multiprofile and confirming the scgpt+resnet50+avgpool+concat baseline. The biggest untested lever is the image encoder: ResNet50 (~25M params) vs ImageNet ViT-L (~300M+ params), which is a substantially stronger pretrained visual feature extractor. Question: does upgrading the image encoder to imagenet_vit_l while holding aggregation (avgpool) and fusion (concat) constant yield a meaningful accuracy gain? This is a clean single-variable extension of our current best config. It is the best use of experiment 3 because (a) the image encoder is likely the highest-impact remaining design choice, (b) it isolates one variable so we can attribute any change to the encoder, and (c) the result directly informs which image encoder to pair with other improvements (RNA encoder, fusion) in subsequent experiments. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high (~6-8 GPU hours) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, but still well below the transformer-aggregation cost seen in config_001 (9.06 hrs) since we retain the cheaper avgpool aggregation."
}

